            <!-- EVENT 3 -->
            <section id="event-3" class="event-section">
                <h1 class="event-title">SAW THUNDER HEARD LIGHTING</h1>
                <h2 class="event-subtitle">A MUSIC & ART SHOWCASE</h2>
                <div class="event-meta">JUNE 4TH, 2026 | LINT STUDIOS, LOS ANGELES</div>
                
                <div class="event-layout" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">
                    <div class="event-main">
                        
                        <!-- Images Above Description -->
                        <div class="image-grid" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                            <img src="0604_STHL.png" alt="STHL Flyer">
                            <img src="4Z3A6292.jpg" alt="STHL Documentation">
                        </div>

                        <div class="event-description">
                            <p>At Mount Sinai, <i>"All the people saw the sounds and the lightning, the voice of the horn and the mountain smoking"</i>.</p>
                            <p>Drawing from the sensory and symbolic language of Shavuot, Saw Thunder Heard Lightning brings together musicians and visual artists across five live sets and eight artworks for one night asking: How might sound, sight, scent, and taste touch the time spent in a shared room?</p>
                            <p>Participating artists and performers engage with themes of harvest, joy, reception, and revelation. Exploring the theme of union, each live set was conceived as a collaboration between musicians and artist pairings. Exhibited artworks highlight motifs such as fruit, dairy, lightning, and wheat, across sculpture, natural dyes, edible elements, and site-specific installations.</p>
                            <p>Made in partnership with AFIPO.</p>

                            <h3>PERFORMANCES</h3>
                            <p>AGAT (Vox, Drums, Guitar) x Shawn Law Yone (Violin)<br>
                            Odeya Nini (Vox) x Corey Fogel (Drum Kit & Percussion)<br>
                            Livya Howard-Yashar (Movement & Body Percussion) x Corey Fogel (Drum Kit)<br>
                            Joshua Zeitlin (Trumpet) x Seventh Spiel (Hardware) x Livya Howard-Yashar (Percussion)<br>
                            Alan Niku (Tar) x Jamie Papish (Hand Drum)</p>

                            <h3>ARTISTS / ARTWORKS / DIMENSIONS</h3>
                            <!-- Two column list for artworks -->
                            <div class="two-column-list">
                                <p>Liz Berger<br>Natural dye activation<br>@27339k</p>
                                <p>Adrienne Adar<br>Play the Hands You’re Given, 2026<br>7 channel, live interactive sound sculptures. Dimensions variable.<br>Materials: Bronze, Plant Material (rosemary, fern), handmade electronics, mixer, speaker.<br>@adrienneadar</p>
                                <p>Kim Kyne Cohen<br>Born Again, 2026<br>NFS, glaze, underglaze & acrylic on ceramic<br>14x12.5"<br><br>Strawberry 2024 glazed ceramic<br>13” x 7” x 6"<br>@kimkynecohen</p>
                                <p>Masha Sheinina<br>Sex Pot, 2024 Ceramic, nichrome wire, lusters<br>18” x 19” x 19”<br>@kakashaceramics</p>
                                <p>Ari Salka & Chris Gwillim<br>Study of Partial Unfolding & Study of an Unfolding, 2026<br>Canvas, Pigment, Metal<br>Dimensions Variable<br>@drawingwithpaint<br>Both works are site-responsive and may be adapted to different architectural conditions</p>
                                <p>Irina Skorynyakova<br>Lightning<br>2026<br>14” D x 37” W x 5’7” H<br>Steel, rock from pisgah crater, candle</p>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Back to single column -->
                            <p><i>“The manifestation of “Lightning” came through welding, a process that feels like a literal attempt to control electrical energy. There is something inherently magical in this act of transforming electricity into form. The sculpture extends toward the heavens, catching what comes from above through a candle, while simultaneously rooting itself into the ground. It becomes a meeting point between forces above and below, between electricity and flame, earth and sky, the physical and the metaphysical.”</i> - Irina Skorynyakova</p>

                            <h3>TEAM</h3>
                            <p>Bobby Guevara, Eric Penea - Sound<br>
                            Joseph Hu - Art Handling<br>
                            Omer Yousef - Creative Tech<br>
                            Shelly Badal - Curator, Producer</p>
                        </div>

